{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Mynavathi (26 July 1935 – 10 November 2012) was an Indian film and television actress.","title":"Mynavathi"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" She made her first screen appearance as an actor in the 1955 Kannada film "Santa Sakhu" and acted in over 100 Kannada films.","title":"Mynavathi"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" She was the younger sister of another popular Kannada actress Pandari Bai.","title":"Mynavathi"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" She became popular after her role in the 1959 Kannada film "Abba Aa Hudugi", which co-starred Rajkumar and her sister Pandari Bai and was directed by H.L.N. Simha.","title":"Mynavathi"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" In the film, she played the role of an autocratic girl who hates men.","title":"Mynavathi"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" It was based on William Shakespeare's play "The Taming of the Shrew".","title":"Mynavathi"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Taming of the Shrew is a comedy by William Shakespeare, believed to have been written between 1590 and 1592.","title":"The Taming of the Shrew"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Arun Sagar (born 23 October 1965) is an Indian film actor, art director and comedian who mainly works in the Kannada film industry.","title":"Arun Sagar"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" He has been recognized as a leading art director throughout his career starting from his first movie, "Bhoomi Geetha" which won the national award for best environmental film.","title":"Arun Sagar"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" He has worked with veteran directors like Poori Jagannath, Meher Ramesh, Veerashankar and K Raghavendra Rao.","title":"Arun Sagar"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" He has received Karnataka state award for best art direction for his contributions in the movie Sri Manjunatha.","title":"Arun Sagar"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" He ran a show on Kasturi TV called 'Tarrle' that resembled a popular show "M.A.D." from Pogo TV that taught children about art, painting and crafting.","title":"Arun Sagar"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" He became popular during the telecast of "Maja with Sruja" that aired on Asianet Suvarna where he played various comical roles that parodied celebrities and politicians.","title":"Arun Sagar"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" The show was a huge hit for its satire-comedy structure.","title":"Arun Sagar"},{"sentence_id":7,"text":" Arun Sagar was later roped in as the first contestant of Bigg Boss Kannada Season 1, where he emerged as the runner-up for the season.","title":"Arun Sagar"},{"sentence_id":8,"text":" He later reprised the comedy genre with a new show, "Comedy Circle" that was aired on ETV Kannada.","title":"Arun Sagar"},{"sentence_id":9,"text":" The show was successful, however for unknown reasons, he opted out of the show after few episodes.","title":"Arun Sagar"},{"sentence_id":10,"text":" He also hosted a one-man-show on the same genre known as "Koyyam Kotra" on TV9 (Kannada).","title":"Arun Sagar"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Ragini (Ragini) Nandwani (born 4 September 1989) is an Indian film and television actress.","title":"Ragini Nandwani"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" She became popular after playing the lead in the Hindi soap opera "Mrs. Kaushik Ki Paanch Bahuein" (2011–12).","title":"Ragini Nandwani"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" She made her Bollywood debut with the crime thriller film "Dehraadun Diary" (2013) which was based on a real murder case.","title":"Ragini Nandwani"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Abba Aa Hudugi (Kannada: ಅಬ್ಬಾ ಆ ಹುಡುಗಿ ) is a 1959 Indian Kannada film directed and produced by H. L. N. Sinha.","title":"Abba Aa Hudugi"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Its stars Rajkumar, Mynavathi and Pandari Bai in lead roles.","title":"Abba Aa Hudugi"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" It is considered a landmark film in Kannada cinema.","title":"Abba Aa Hudugi"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Andrzej Zbylitowski was born "ca."","title":"Andrzej Zbylitowski"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" 1565, probably in Zagorzyce, Świętokrzyskie Voivodeship, as a son of Stanisław and Jadwiga Rożnówna, and also a first cousin of Piotr Zbylitowski.","title":"Andrzej Zbylitowski"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" After he finished studies abroad, he back to the country, and in 1585 became a courtier on the royal court of Stefan Batory, and later of Zygmunt III Waza.","title":"Andrzej Zbylitowski"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" In 1592 he became a Master of the Pantry of the Crown (Polish: "stolnik nadworny" ).","title":"Andrzej Zbylitowski"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" In his political views, he was a follower of Jan Zamoyski.","title":"Andrzej Zbylitowski"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" As a political poet known for his surname, he became popular during the "sejm" in the years of 1590–1591.","title":"Andrzej Zbylitowski"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" Zbylitowski was a very productive court poet, his most notable political works includes 1587 welcoming writing for Zygmunt III Waza who was back to Rzeczpospolita, congratulatory poem for Battle of Byczyna "O zwycięstwie osiągniętym w r. 1588", today unknown poem for Anna of Finland "Pisanie satyrów puszcz litewskich... o łowach w Białobieżach" (1589), "Epithalamium na wesele... Zygmuntowi III i arcyksiężnie JM rakuskiej Annie" (1592) and 1595 genethliacon for the occasion of prince Władysław baptism.","title":"Andrzej Zbylitowski"},{"sentence_id":7,"text":" In 1593 Zbylitowski travelled to Sweden with companion of Zygmunt III Waza, and depicted that travel in poem "Droga do Szwecyjej namożniejszego w północnych krainach Pana, Zygmunta III, polskiego i szwedzkiego króla, odprawiona w roku 1594", published later in 1597 by Jakub Siebeneicher.","title":"Andrzej Zbylitowski"},{"sentence_id":8,"text":" In "ca."","title":"Andrzej Zbylitowski"},{"sentence_id":9,"text":" 1597 he settled in Zbylitowska Góra where he wrote two rural poems: "Żywot szlachcica we wsi" (1597) and "Wieśniak" (1600).","title":"Andrzej Zbylitowski"}],"peer_messages":["Unverified peer answer: William Shakespeare
